WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.259
When I first got into education a
quarter-century ago, it was frighteningly

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:13.940
easy to find teachers and schools who
shrugged off responsibility for kids who

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.870
weren't learning. It was too easy to
blame the home or the family. Happily,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:22.100
things have changed. Today, when you go to
schools and systems, you find teachers

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:26.090
being asked to take responsibility for
every one of their charges. That's a

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:30.470
fantastic thing. Here's the problem:
Teachers don't work alone. They work in

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:34.940
partnership with families; with students.
We need to make sure that teachers are

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.079
not being asked to shoulder the whole
burden. The KIPP charter schools have a

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:42.050
wonderful model of how to deal with this:
They have a Commitment to Excellence

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:49.160
that is signed by teacher, student, and
parent, in which they are all asked to take

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:52.970
responsibility for making sure the
student succeeds. What we need are

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.680
schools where teachers are asked to do
all that they can for every child, but

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.930
that also expects parents and families to
step up and be partners for the schools,

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.400
to ensure that each child is well served.

